welcome everybody to the closing  ceremony of the st louis rapid and blitz  the fourth stop of the 2022 grand chess  tour my name is christian carrillo and i  will be your host tonight first of all i  would like to start by acknowledging  shannon bailey and her staff here at the  world chess hall of fame for putting  this closing ceremony together as well  as for bringing the history and culture  of chess through the exhibitions  here at the world chess hall of fame  i would also like to thank two people  without which  none of this would be possible uh  through their love for chess as well as  the city of saint louis they have  created something magical here in saint  louis the best chess club in the world  of course i'm talking about dr ginny and  rex sinfield  [Applause]  i would also like to thank the visionary  behind the grand chester  a man that is synonymous with the word  chess that is of course mr gary kasparov  [Applause]  and of course i would also like to thank  three people that simply get things done  the executive director of the grand  chester michael kodakovsky the executive  director of the saint louis chess club  tony rich and the general manager of the  saint louis chess campus joy bray  congratulations guys  [Applause]  and of course none of this would be  possible without strong partnerships and  i would like to highlight our partner in  europe superbad as well as our partner  here in st louis the st louis chess club  and without further ado i will give the  word to the big dog tony rich  tony  [Applause]  thank you  thank you very much christian and thank  you all so much for joining us here at  the closing ceremony of the 2022 st  louis rapid and blitz  just briefly i mentioned at the opening  ceremony why you don't want to become a  super grand master right it's hard you  travel all the time you study all the  time it's painful to lose the games but  on the other hand there are lots of  great reasons why you should become a  super grand master  for one alariza has proven to us that  five days of work can earn you forty  thousand dollars that's not too bad at  all  on top of that you get to travel the  world see new places meet new people  enjoy the culture the food  and the camaraderie that comes with  being one of the best chess players  along with your fellow compatriots so  any chess players out there i encourage  you to stick with the game enjoy it and  if you become a super grand master  stop by the chess club and play even if  you don't become a super grand master  stop by the chess club and play  it's my pleasure now to introduce to you  the uh the lady who is responsible for  the chess club over the past 15 years  she and her husband rex have been the  guiding force  behind what we do here in st louis dr  jeanne singfield  [Applause]  thank you tony hey this has been a great  tournament  anyways looking at all the players that  are here  obviously there's a lot who are playing  for america who come from a variety of  other places but this is probably one of  the most interesting  international based on where people were  born seven were born  seven different countries  lots of different people a lot of them  keep trying to come to america and live  in uh you know  st louis city the chess place but what  can i say we're the chess place  so it's it's a very cool group and i  also wanted to point out  our winter  today you know how he really learned  chess  watching  the chess tournaments from the u.s chess  club and watching our videos see you  guys are playing and you're not  listening  so that's sort of cool isn't it  to have someone literally been watching  our tournament since we started  well anyway so we're having fun  and uh it's time for me to introduce rex  so when you if you think about it given  how  lousy a chess player i am and  and he's somewhat better  and can i tell my one joke  one joke when we first got married  he wanted to play chess and i said that  was okay  i mean how expensive could it be  and let me introduce the godfather of  american chess  rex infield  thank you very much genie i'll erase it  i watched our tournaments all the time  nothing great happened to me  so  it's always exciting when someone's  playing in st louis  for the first time and wins the  tournament wow this one was a big  big example of that congratulations ola  razer for your amazing performance in  the tournament  you played outstanding chess and  clinched your win early today  genie and i and the staff are very happy  for you and your victory  i would also like to thank the best  commentary team in the world i always  say this because it's true  and for the wonderful job they did with  rapid and blitz grand master yasser  cerewon peter svidler christian chorilla  and women's grand master anastasia  carlovich  [Applause]  the staff at the chess club in the world  chess hall of fame  uh work very well together and do a  phenomenal job day in and day out  they don't nearly get the accolades they  deserve but thanks to tony rich the  executive director shannon bailey the  chief curator of the world chess hall of  fame  and the one that holds it all together  for everyone joy bray  [Music]  [Applause]  i also want to thank the contractors who  do so much work for us  randy and his team at spectrum studios  kevin deputy and his crew at silverback  and the st louis chess club production  team thank you all  so  [Applause]  i have to say it was amazing to watch  alareza and ricardo dominate rapid and  blitz  they both gained a lot of rating points  they're now over 2 900  ricardo congratulations on being number  one in the world in blitz and  congratulations  congratulations to both you and alareza  for an outstanding performance thank you  [Applause]  thank you rex  and one more time i would like to  acknowledge my partners in crime the  players had a lot of fun but we had a  lot of fun as well  legends of chess commentary yasser  sarawan and peter svidler please stand  up  [Applause]  and of course woman grandmaster  anastasia carlovich for relaying the  emotions of the players the commentators  through her stories her interviews thank  you very much anastasia  [Applause]  and now it's time to get uh down to  business it's time to award the victors  we're going to start with third and  fourth place we have a two-way tie  between fabiano caruana and maxim vashir  lagrav both of them  please stand up guys  please stand up guys  both of them have earned  [Applause]  a cool  22.5 thousand dollars and 7.5 grand  chess tour points  a man  with a legion of fans in the second  place  a subpar performance for him in the  rapid portion but he showed who the man  is in the blitz section of course i'm  talking about hikaru nakamura  [Applause]  and of course  the young phenom from france  the winner of the 2022 saint louis rapid  and blitz ali reza firuja  [Applause]  ali raza please a few words  yes thank you christian  yeah it's of course um it's a dream come  true for me to win a tournament in saint  louis  i always had the dream to come to play  here but  the bigger dream was to win a tournament  here so i'm really happy to have done  that  and  yeah i want to really thank the  organizer  for all the great efforts to do the  chess tournaments it's a difficult job  really to do  and i want to thank  dr ginny and rex for  um  everything that they've done for chess  so  um and i'm  yeah i'm really looking forward to  playing sing field cup that is coming up  very soon  thank you  once again the winner of the 2022 saint  louis rapid and blitz ali reza ferruga  congratulations alireza  well this is it for us tonight we're  going to conclude the closing ceremony  thank you very much and we will see you  in just a couple of days with the  opening ceremony of the sinful cup until  then goodbye and good night  [Applause]  [Music]  you

